   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# POLS 2100\n",
    "\n",
    "## Week 3 Activity Notebook 2: Data visualization\n",
    "\n",
    "In this activity, you will be practicing scatterplot visualizations on your own.\n",
    "\n",
    "Let's start by reading in data from Broockman and Skovron (2018)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a85d37ef-622a-43ca-bf12-4d02a22fe1a9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "library(testthat)\n",
    "library(ggplot2); options(warn=-1)\n",
    "options(repr.plot.width = 4, repr.plot.height = 3, repr.plot.res = 50)\n",
    "\n",
    "data <- read.csv('broockman_skovron.csv')[1:750,]\n",
    "head(data)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4cc4de24-c9f6-4b4a-848b-83e317bebb0c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Here is an overview of what the columns in the dataset represent: \n",
    "\n",
    "- `republican`: whether the state legislator or state legislative candidate who answered the survey was a Republican (1 = Republican, 0 = Democrat)\n",
    "- `incumbent`: whether the person who answered the survey was an incumbent representative (i.e., currently holds political office) (1 = already holds office, 0 = just a candidate)\n",
    "- `marriage_perception`: what percent of the politician's constituents they think support same-sex marriage\n",
    "- `marriage_opinion`: what percent of the politician's constituents actually support same-sex marriage\n",
    "- `religexempt_perception`: what percent of the politician's constituents they think support allowing employers to refuse to cover birth control for employees if it violates their religious beliefs\n",
    "- `religexempt_opinion`: what percent of the politician's constituents actually support allowing employers to refuse to cover birth control for employees if it violates their religious beliefs\n",
    "- `gunsbanassault_perception`: what percent of the politician's constituents they think support banning assault weapons\n",
    "- `gunsbanassault_opinion`: what percent of the politician's constituents actually support banning assault weapons"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "920708df-86e5-4beb-a964-99e2c94356ca",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# BEGIN QUESTION\n",
    "name: q1\n",
    "points: 1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "72be2d40-ddef-4315-889b-ff0f545a6e8d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "------\n",
    "\n",
    "**Question 1. Make a scatterplot _among Democratic legislators only_ where actual constituency support for same-sex marriage is on the x-axis and perceived constituency support for it is on the y-axis.**\n",
    "\n",
    "To do this, first subset the data to Democratic legislators (i.e., where `republican` is 0) and save the data in the `democrats.only` subset.\n",
    "\n",
    "Then, make a graph with `marriage_opinion` on the x axis and `marriage_perception` on the y axis, within the `democrats.only` dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "_Do not_ include a line of best fit yet."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "5073a6f2-b4dd-4a72-a493-467ed38e1515",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# BEGIN SOLUTION"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2321f346-4a23-465b-83e2-8f7384be3d89",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# First, subset the data to Democratic legislators only\n",
    "democrats.only <- subset(data, republican == 0) # SOLUTION\n",
    "\n",
    "# Now, make a scatter plot with marriage_opinion on the x axis and marriage_perception on the y axis,\n",
    "# within the democrats.only dataset\n",
    "dem.graph <- ggplot(democrats.only, aes(x = marriage_opinion, y = marriage_perception)) + geom_point() # SOLUTION\n",
    "\n",
    "dem.graph # Let's look at the graph. (This might take a couple seconds to run.)"
   ]
  },
